  "mechanical_coverage": "MECHANICAL: 361 historical ACT report sections in the committed root board were mechanically indexed by identity, verdict and exact source range into 316 distinct historical ACT identities (289 UNAMBIGUOUS, 2 AMBIGUOUS, 25 CONFLICTING). The extraction indexes BOTH report-section heading levels: the level-1 prepend-ordered report log AND the level-2 report sections of the trailing board region, which the previous level-1-only extraction silently skipped (149 identities, including 18 with competing verdicts). Every competing verdict is retained with its own source reference; no identity is silently deduplicated.",
  "semantic_coverage": "SEMANTIC: 21 actual epics and 45 engineering obligations were reconciled from the committed epic detail files and the board's operational index. The board's Current frontier / Active epics / Open supporting work / Deferred-hold tables were reconciled lane-by-lane; the per-epic Open work and Deferred work sections were reconciled obligation-by-obligation. Where the source represents ONE obligation in several places, exactly ONE representation is authoritative and the others are conserved as source accounting (secondary representations) and reconciliation records, so no source representation is lost and no obligation is scheduled twice. The remaining narrative history (the board's report prose and `Updated:` chronology lines, the multi-ACT closure narratives in command-risk-classification.md, webview-seam-aop.md and context-compaction-token-accounting.md, and the long Current-status bullets in safe-yolo-seatbelt.md) was accounted for as contiguous narrative history at the byte level and is preserved verbatim in the committed source archive. It is deliberately NOT reconstructed as new work items. The board's trailing region 9,542-44,731 is accounted for in full; it carries 205 further report sections belonging to 149 historical identities, all of which are now indexed."
